his round is explicitly 're-verification of the git -C chain-leak fix (commit 3a90bd0)' only -- it does not re-examine or close the other two findings from the same prior review.; Verified separately that the git -C chain-leak finding is correctly fixed at this HEAD: _resolution_walk's git -C branch (lines 416-430) now computes a part-local base/base_nl and no longer reassigns the shared current/nonliteral the rest of the chain loop reads, matching the new tests test_shell_guard_git_dash_c_does_not_leak_into_a_later_chain_part and test_shell_guard_resolves_a_git_dash_c_target and verifier.md's live subprocess runs. That part of the fix is sound and is not grounds for escalation by itself; the escalation rests on the other two, still-open gaps from the same review round.",
